{"skill":{"slug":"daily-report","displayName":"Daily Report"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770291915487,"changelog":"- Initial release of daily-report skill, providing automated daily, end-of-day, and weekly reporting templates.\n- Tracks lead pipeline, outreach, metrics, and budget in structured reports.\n- Saves daily log summaries to memory files for future reference.\n- Includes support for immediate alerts on replies, budget thresholds, API errors, and blockers.\n- Designed for use with a local ollama model for cost-free, simple aggregation.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2202,"sha256":"8221b27c4375065999aa1112b43f61287bf25ee56b64210837a48e0140c282bd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2148,"sha256":"6ee0cca7dfd3c36ef6bb0cb5ce43749a44767b8c5cc27d46444e3be385b8648b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789034783641,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"6b7788a69fda9c78fcbf4a9e770e3290f8770ff3cfa9feacd3710071fd6be719","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/6b7788a69fda9c78fcbf4a9e770e3290f8770ff3cfa9feacd3710071fd6be719","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\n\nThe skill bundle defines reporting templates, memory management, and alert mechanisms. It instructs the agent to save operational logs to local files (e.g., `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`) and send operational alerts via Telegram. These file write and network communication actions are explicitly stated in `SKILL.md` and are directly aligned with the stated purpose of 'Track progress, report metrics, manage memory'. There is no evidence of intent to exfiltrate sensitive data, execute malicious commands, establish persistence, or perform unauthorized actions beyond the skill's stated functionality.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161551826},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":20,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789034783641},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a simple daily reporting skill with disclosed local logs and Telegram alerts, with privacy and timezone settings users should review.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Telegram alerts are explicitly instructed for operational events, creating an external notification data flow that is purpose-aligned but should be configured to avoid sending sensitive lead, budget, or error details.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No executable scripts, dependencies, installers, hooks, or remote payload retrieval were present; metadata is empty and the package contains only the markdown skill artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The reporting times use a fixed Spain timezone without describing configurability, which is limiting but not deceptive or unsafe.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill directs daily markdown logs under memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; this local persistence is disclosed and coherent with reporting, but retention and deletion controls are not described.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to track progress, report metrics, and manage memory, and the artifact only contains report templates, metrics, local log format, and alert triggers aligned with that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, confirm you want reports on the listed Spain-time schedule, configure Telegram only if that channel is approved for your business data, and periodically review or delete the local memory logs if they contain operational details.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The Telegram alert behavior is explicitly stated and fits operational reporting, but users should limit alert content to minimal sanitized metadata.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Spain timezone schedule is visible in the artifact and is a usability/configuration limitation rather than a security-policy concern requiring Review.\n[SQP-2] expected: The local memory file writes are part of the stated memory/reporting purpose and are documented in the template, though retention guidance is missing.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789034783641}}}}}